[statement]
A package displaced goes, at the latest, just before the walk placing the
package that displaces it, after the removals still waiting on it: `new`
takes `v` from the installed `old`, which the kept `k` needs, and `w`,
removed, needs `old`; `w` itself would go last, since `y` needed it
through `u`, a name it provides at a version. apk removes `w`, then
`old`, after `a` and `b`, just before installing `new`.

[repository]
P:new
V:1
p:v=2

P:app
V:1
D:a b new

P:a
V:1

P:b
V:1

[installed]
P:old
V:1
p:v=1

P:w
V:1
p:u=1
D:old

P:y
V:1
D:u

P:k
V:1
D:v

[world]
k

[request]
app

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
remove y 1
install a 1
install b 1
remove w 1
remove old 1
install new 1
install app 1
